- do NOT write .cu, .cpp, .py, or any implementation code
- do NOT create build scripts, Makefiles, or test files
- do NOT push to any git repository
- ONLY output: ## MODULE headers + LAYER 1a (LaTeX) + LAYER 1b (Lean 4) + LAYER 2 (form template)
- write theory as TEXT in your response, or use create_file for .md files only
- STOP when you have covered every file in YOUR assignment. do NOT look for more files.

you may use git to read other files for CONTEXT (understanding types, interfaces, dependencies).
the bare repo is at /tmp/ref_Niko1221_Strata.git — use `git --git-dir=/tmp/ref_Niko1221_Strata.git show 01529aaa82b9:<path>`.
but produce LAYER 1/2 ONLY for YOUR assigned files. when those are done, you are done.
if any single file is too large to fully analyze, list its functions and produce both layers for the most important ones.

