```

And the ordering contract from lines 20+:

```
///     ring -> hits(Launch)   [GPU: quantize + grouped experts into `hit_out`]
///          -> pool()         [CPU: the misses, CONCURRENT with the GPU]
///          -> H2D misses into `parts`
///          -> hits(Combine)  [GPU: parts += hit_out]
///          -> post[l]
```

The **Combine** phase adds `hit_out` into `parts` (not just a query — it does `parts += hit_out`). This is a crucial detail. Let me also note the measurement context: the first version called the hit path once after the pool, writing straight into `parts`, and "the drain duly fell 18.2 → 10.2 ms — the CPU really was doing half the experts — and the token did not move at all" because the GPU's half had been serialized. The two-phase design (Launch concurrent with pool, Combine after) fixes this.

